THE EVIDENCE BOUNDARY

What this run supports - and what it does not.

OBSERVED                                                             NOT ESTABLISHED

• End-to-end workflow on one authored scenario.                      • General accuracy, precision or recall.
• Local Llama candidate facts; deterministic parsing and traversal.  • Time saved vs manual work.
• Four grounding states, including adjacent-line context.            • Unique AI-only raw facts.
• Human rejection of one false-positive relationship.                • Real customer data, demand or pilots.
• Deferred alias; confirmed vs possible scope; export.               • Production readiness, OCR or certification.

                                             One authored scenario · one local model · one operator · n=1

                                                                    We are deliberately showing the boundary, not hiding it.

Klarrow · evidence-reconciliation workbench                                                                                   07
SOUTH AFRICAN CONTEXT

Why this matters in South Africa.

Producer responsibility                                     Export traceability                                                 Regulator can require action

Food safety and accurate labelling rest with the producer.  PPECB food-safety audits explicitly cover traceability for          The NCC may require a producer to conduct an
Enforcement is delegated to municipal health services.      regulated agricultural products intended for export.                investigation or carry out a recall programme on its
                                                                                                                                terms.

National Department of Health, Food Control                 PPECB, Food Safety Services                                         Consumer Protection Act 68 of 2008, s60

The implication: one event may need an evidence pack for several audiences. We are testing whether an evidence-reconciliation overlay helps - not claiming
that demand is proven.

Sources: health.gov.za/food-control-home · ppecb.com/services/food-safety-services · gov.za Consumer Protection Act 68 of 2008

